	<h2>Disciple of Munger</h2>
	<p>
		I am a devoted student of Charlie Munger's timeless investment philosophy. His principles of clear thinking, behavioral discipline, and rational decision-making have fundamentally shaped my approach to wealth creation and business analysis. Kuberin represents my commitment to applying Munger's four pillars—MOAT, MANAGEMENT, MARGIN, and MOMENTUM—to identify extraordinary investment opportunities.
	</p>

	<h2>Multidisciplinary Thinking & First Principles</h2>
	<p>
		My competitive edge stems from a multidisciplinary approach grounded in first-principles thinking. Rather than accepting conventional wisdom, I deconstruct complex problems to their foundational truths, allowing me to see opportunities that others miss. By integrating knowledge from physics, biology, economics, psychology, and technology, I've developed a unique lens for evaluating businesses and identifying transformational companies before they become obvious to the mainstream.
	</p>

	<h2>Compounding Through Multibaggers</h2>
	<p>
		My investment journey has been defined by identifying and holding multibagger opportunities—stocks that have returned 10x, 40x, or more. Early recognition of paradigm-shifting companies like Tesla and SpaceX, combined with the discipline to hold through volatility, has been crucial to my wealth compounding. These weren't lucky guesses; they were deliberate applications of first-principles analysis combined with pattern recognition from studying business history. The power of compound wealth comes not just from returns, but from holding long enough to let the exponential curve work its magic.
	</p>

